      "math_academy_id": "e-15059",
      "problem": "Using the cumulative distribution function table of the Poisson random variable $X \\sim \\textrm{Po}(8)$ given below, compute $P(3 \\leq X \\leq 6).$\n\n| $\\quad x \\quad$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ | $7$ | $8$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $P(X\\leq x)$ | $\\,0.0138\\,$ | $\\,0.0424\\,$ | $\\,0.0996\\,$ | $\\,0.1912\\,$ | $\\,0.3134\\,$ | $\\,0.4530\\,$ | $\\,0.5925\\,$ |",
      "worked_solution": "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x) = P(X \\leq x).\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(6) & =P(X\\le 6) \\\\  & =P(X\\in \\{0,1,…,6\\}) \\\\  & =P(X\\in \\{0,1,2\\})+P(X\\in \\{3,4,5,6\\}) \\\\  & =P(X\\le 2)+P(3\\le X\\le 6) \\\\  & =F(2)+P(3\\le X\\le 6).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(3\\le X\\le 6) & =F(6)-F(2) \\\\  & =0.3134-0.0138 \\\\  & =0.2996.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
